      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Blood meal generally has a significantly higher nitrogen percentage than bone meal, with very low phosphorus and potassium. Regarding leaching, because blood meal is a quick-release organic source, it can be prone to leaching if heavily applied or if frequent, heavy rain occurs. To mitigate this risk, apply it in smaller, more frequent top-dressings instead of one large application.",
